# {{TITLE}} – film project

This project is cut with **cutter**. The rules and the cut cycle are in the `video-editing` skill
(Claude Code: `cutter:video-editing`, Codex: `$video-editing`) and in `docs/` of the cutter repository
({{CUTTER_HOME}}). This file holds the facts of this project. Talk to the user in the user's language.

## Facts

- Project folder: `{{PROJECT}}`
- Footage (read only, never change it; mounted read-only in the container):
{{MEDIA}}
- License of the film: {{LICENSE}}
- Music: allowed {{ALLOWED}} (cutter.toml → music.allowed_licenses). Check before use: `{{CUTTER}} music license`.
  ND and BY-SA are never allowed. If the tags say nothing, ask the user.
- Review app: {{REVIEW_URL}}
- Analysis: `analysis/clips.json`, transcripts `analysis/transcripts/<clip>.json`, contact sheets `analysis/sheets/`
- Cuts: `cuts/cut<n>/` with `edit.json`, `decisions.json`, `plan.py` (from cut2 on), timeline files, `cut<n>.fcproj`
- Exports: `exports/cut<n>.mp4`; review data and passwords: `.cutter/` (private)

## Commands

```sh
{{CUTTER}} doctor                        # check the setup
{{CUTTER}} analyze                       # clips, transcripts, contact sheets (long: run in the background)
{{CUTTER}} music license                 # licenses of music/* against cutter.toml
{{CUTTER}} music analyze                 # beats, bars, loudness -> music/music.json
{{CUTTER}} plan cut2 --new               # feedback as code: cuts/cut2/plan.py
{{CUTTER}} plan cut2                     # -> cuts/cut2/edit.json
{{CUTTER}} retime cut2                   # cuts on the beat
{{CUTTER}} timeline cut2                 # audio levels, .otio/.fcp7.xml/.srt
{{CUTTER}} filmcraft build cut2          # FilmCraft project cuts/cut2/cut2.fcproj (headless)
{{CUTTER}} filmcraft export cut2         # exports/cut2.mp4, subtitles burned in
{{CUTTER}} review-data cut2              # uses exports/cut2.mp4 if it exists
{{CUTTER}} review password <name>        # the user types the password (only a hash is stored)
{{CUTTER}} serve                         # review app in the home network (ask first)
{{CUTTER}} feedback fetch                # comments on the newest cut -> .cutter/review/feedback-<cut>.json
{{CUTTER}} feedback reply cut2 --file replies.json
```

Every command accepts `--json`; commands that write, render or deploy accept `--dry-run`.

## Rules for this project

- Never change the footage and never write into it. New files only in the project folder.
- Ask the user before large downloads (Docker image, Whisper model), `sudo`, changes to the shell configuration
  or to `~/.claude` / `~/.codex` / `~/.agents`, deploying, and deleting anything.
- Only feedback on the newest cut counts. Every cut gets `cuts/cut<n>/decisions.json`.
- Always subtitle dialogue; burn the subtitles in on export.
- Use the "mild" audio chain for dialogue (the full chain sounded tinny).
- Never run browser tests of the review app against real data.
